00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start position:0%
a local woman is grieving tonight after  her husband set fire to their home and  took his own life she and her four  children are now without a place to live  tonight victoria saha takes a look at  how suicide impacts those left behind  and the options available for those  suffering he's a really funny guy cora  williams is remembering her husband  jerome williams of 11 years the  childhood sweethearts share four  children together he really loved his  children so much he really did which is  why cora never thought her family would  ever be living this nightmare on july 7  cora got a chilling text from jerome  showing a picture of their house on fire  and then he texted  that this was the last time i'd hear  from him  he told me  to tell the kids that he loved them and  that he was sorry but it was too late  the family says jerome had set their  house on fire then took his own life i  just don't think he was really in his  right  mindset cora tells me it was only after  her husband's passing that she found out  he was diagnosed with bipolar depression  when he was younger but never got help  for it i knew that he did struggle  but i think he really was more like  ashamed and  didn't want to seek the help a problem  brewing for many people suffering from  mental illness according to karen  esposito a psychiatrist with roseman  university people who are dealing with  mental health issues  can  reach a moment of crisis really at any  time which is why the new suicide  hotline number 988 is so crucial giving  someone the chance to talk it out the  most important thing is to have someone  to listen to in the moment to give some  thoughts and guidance and direction as  for cora she hopes her story can be a  turning point for those suffering in  silence but for right now the mama 4 is  trying to push forward  one day at a time i just feel like i'm  trying to survive each day victoria zaha  live local now  again if you or someone you know is  experiencing suicidal thoughts call 988  that is the new three-digit number for  the suicide and crisis lifeline and as  for the williams family a gofundme has  been set up to help them we have that  link on our website eightnewsnow.com
 

